# STAR WARS: Squadrons community server mod
# Rule of thumb: our own source, scripts and notes go in; game files, third-party tools, build output and
# anything with personal data (logs, addresses) stay out. Players bring their own copy of the game.

# --- Game files and data extracted from them (never redistribute) ---
# copy of the game exe, Ghidra project, decompiler output
work/
# EBX dumps and other data extracted from the game
out/
*.exe.bak
*.toc
*.sb
*.cas
*.cat

# --- Third-party tools and reference code (download separately; Kyber is GPLv3, reference only) ---
ext/
refs/

# --- Build output ---
probe/build/
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib
*.dll
*.exe
# packaged test builds (zips); publish builds as GitHub releases instead
release/

# --- Logs and live configs (IP addresses, Tailscale addresses, Windows user names) ---
probe_logs/
logs/
*.status.txt
probe_*.bin
rules_*.bin
server_*.bin
# live configs: commit *.example.ini versions instead
server.ini
rules.ini
launch.ini

# --- Generated from the game data by tools/ (regenerate rather than commit) ---
unlock_ids.txt
notes/sws_runtime_types.json
notes/sws_sdk_types.json
notes/customization-catalog.json

# --- Python ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Local tool and editor state ---
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/output-styles/
.vscode/
.vs/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Ported from Frosty Toolsuite (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0: no derivatives) and the scripts built on it.
# Kept out of the public repo until the Frosty authors agree or the reader is rewritten from format notes.
tools/frostbite/
tools/swsdata.py
tools/customization_catalog.py
tools/unlock_ids.py
tools/fbsdk.py
tools/dump_sdk_types.py
